#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# finite_abelian_group_count

#% text
# `finite_abelian_group_count(k)` gives the number of abelian groups of order `k` up to isomorphism, the product of `partitions_p(e)` over the prime powers `p^e` exactly dividing `k`.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
finite_abelian_group_count(range(1, 12))
#% output
#= [1, 1, 1, 2, 1, 1, 1, 3, 2, 1, 1, 2]

#% cell
finite_abelian_group_count(2^10*3^5)
#% output
#= 294

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `finite_group_count`, `partitions_p`
